<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=1744&lastnode_id=2040">Dizeez</a> on 2001-07-17 12:23:25</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>As some of you may be aware, someone by the name of Dhamphele has been disparaging the Horde in Shout. What is the protocol for resolving this in a duel? I know I may be out matched in lvls, but I cannot stand by and listen to this Harot. I would not want to make the horde look bad, however, so I waited.</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr>

<tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=2041&lastnode_id=2040">Re: Disrespect for Bloodhorde.</a> (1 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=192&lastnode_id=2040">Runja</a> on 2001-07-17 14:00:31</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>Dis Dahmpeele haz been a thorn in da side of da horde for looooooong time.  She seems ta come and go (disappearing fer months only ta return and continue herz trash talk).<br>
<br>
Me would suggest asking herz whut she gots problem wiff.  If she can only come up wit generalizations (ie "Everybody in Bloodhorde is dishonorable"), ask fer specifics.  Ask whut makes us so bad.  Me sure she will not have any good reasons and will prolly just continue her generalizations.  At this point you should point out dat all she has is generalizations and any problem she haz is not us, but a problem wit herself.   Me sure she would be willing to accept a duel at dat point.  *Grins eviliy*<br>
<br>
Be honorable and mature.  Try ta get her to lose her wit.  Dat would be da best way ta handle dis puss of orc mucus.<br>
<br>
RARR!<br>
 Runja</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr>
</table>
